# colormap: shows the colours of a colour list file as a row of swatches in a window of its own. meta l opens its file dialog; the name
# typed is -, which colrlist reads as standard input (colormap.in, sixteen colour names and one hex value); Return loads it, the swatch
# window opens at 0 0 and the interface is raised over it; meta q quits. The pointer is moved into the dialog before the name is typed.
# Left out: snapshot (meta s), which asks a file name and writes an image; reload, which does nothing in this program.
move 100 150
wait
keydown Alt_L
key l
keyup Alt_L
wait
move 200 134
type -
wait
key Return
wait
move 100 150
keydown Alt_L
key q
keyup Alt_L
